    N: "<div class=\"center\">\xe5 kj\xf8pe<br>kj\xf8per<br>kj\xf8pte<br>har kj\xf8pt</div>",
    E: "<div class=\"center\">to buy, bought, have bought</div>",
    D: "TOP 40 VERBS",
    X: "<div class=\"center\"><div class=\"left\"><p>Remember that the sound of KJ is <span class=\"italic\">similar</span> to the <b class=\"bold\">H</b> in \"<b class=\"bold\">h</b>ue\" and \"<b class=\"bold\">h</b>uge\".</p>This is NOT the same sound as SKJ and SJ, although even natives are at times imprecise about it and some dialects don't differentiate between them.</div></div>",
    A: "N"
